1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,010
Claude Code just closed six

2
00:00:01,810 --> 00:00:03,503
ways a command could slip

3
00:00:03,303 --> 00:00:05,063
past its permission checks.

4
00:00:05,103 --> 00:00:06,824
Many installs do not have

5
00:00:06,624 --> 00:00:07,620
the fixes yet.

6
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:10,313
The stable channel still serves

7
00:00:10,113 --> 00:00:11,841
version two point one point

8
00:00:11,641 --> 00:00:12,771
three one one,

9
00:00:12,571 --> 00:00:14,232
from October twenty-sixth.

10
00:00:14,272 --> 00:00:15,558
Nothing will tell you.

11
00:00:16,108 --> 00:00:17,967
A variable prefix could hide

12
00:00:17,767 --> 00:00:18,962
part of a command.

13
00:00:19,002 --> 00:00:20,601
A new worktree could escape

14
00:00:20,401 --> 00:00:21,184
the sandbox.

15
00:00:21,224 --> 00:00:23,096
An in-place edit skipped the check.

16
00:00:23,646 --> 00:00:25,726
Deny rules missed quoted words.

17
00:00:25,766 --> 00:00:27,681
Rewind followed symlinks out of

18
00:00:27,481 --> 00:00:28,316
your folder.

19
00:00:28,356 --> 00:00:30,587
Untrusted repos could still run

20
00:00:30,387 --> 00:00:32,392
hooks on self-hosted runners.

21
00:00:32,942 --> 00:00:34,888
A booby-trapped repo can steer

22
00:00:34,688 --> 00:00:36,298
the model into a command

23
00:00:36,098 --> 00:00:37,507
the checker misreads.

24
00:00:37,547 --> 00:00:39,272
Anthropic has not said if

25
00:00:39,072 --> 00:00:40,724
any were used in attacks.

26
00:00:40,764 --> 00:00:41,894
Update anyway.

27
00:00:42,444 --> 00:00:44,876
Stable also misses earlier fixes:

28
00:00:44,676 --> 00:00:48,189
resumed worktrees, restricted sessions uploading

29
00:00:47,989 --> 00:00:49,989
outside files, and a check

30
00:00:49,789 --> 00:00:51,574
before sharing your email.

31
00:00:52,124 --> 00:00:53,396
Run claude version.

32
00:00:53,436 --> 00:00:55,045
On the default channel,

33
00:00:54,845 --> 00:00:56,646
run claude update and restart.

34
00:00:56,686 --> 00:00:58,586
On stable, switch to latest

35
00:00:58,386 --> 00:01:00,014
or set a minimum version.

36
00:01:00,564 --> 00:01:02,924
On Homebrew, install the latest cask.

37
00:01:02,964 --> 00:01:05,132
On Linux, point the repository

38
00:01:04,932 --> 00:01:05,694
at latest.

39
00:01:05,734 --> 00:01:07,668
Teams can enforce a required

40
00:01:07,468 --> 00:01:08,640
minimum version.

41
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:10,527
For a tool that holds

42
00:01:10,327 --> 00:01:11,917
a shell on your laptop,

43
00:01:11,717 --> 00:01:13,181
the fresher build may be

44
00:01:12,981 --> 00:01:13,876
the safer one.

45
